# //xr/ui: the command-registry WebUI sources (P7). Lit + strict TypeScript,
# thin views (all logic via the command host protocol).
#
# FARM INTEGRATION PLACEHOLDER (Plan §4 P7: "ui/BUILD.gn placeholder noting
# farm-integration (grit) — no fake integration now"). The real on-tree build
# wires these sources through the Chromium WebUI grit/bundled-resources pipeline
# (content/browser/webui resources) — that is the P16 glue, farm-gated (HG-31).
# There is deliberately NO fake grit/resources target here: a hand-rolled
# .grd/.mojom would be a fake integration the plan explicitly refuses.
#
# Off-tree, the UI is built by the reproducible toolchain (ui/toolchain,
# esbuild) and validated by `tsc --strict` + the CSP/a11y/RTL lints (see
# xr-browser docs/webui-toolchain.md). That toolchain is the "stable for other
# tracks" P7 deliverable; P8/P13 add WebUI through it.

# (Intentionally empty target list — see the farm-integration note above. The
# group exists so //xr/ui is a valid dep target once the P16 grit target lands.)
group("ui_sources_placeholder") {
  # No sources yet: the sources are TypeScript built off-tree by the toolchain.
  # When the P16 farm grit target lands, it replaces this placeholder.
}
